{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>If, etc.</b> May YHWH lead you always. \"If you turn back your foot from the Sabbath\" — or it is joined with \"turning back paths,\" which is also correct. The meaning: from walking on the Sabbath." "<b>Doing your affairs.</b> The meaning is doubled." "<b>And you call the Sabbath a delight.</b> That you not do labor on it, and that the soul take pleasure in hearing words of Torah." "<b>To the holy day of YHWH honored.</b> It is the day of Sabbath. Now the meaning of \"honored\" is explained by the continuation, \"and you honor it, not doing your ways\" — what you are accustomed to do on weekdays; and likewise, (as we find,) [it means] from pursuing your affairs and speaking a word — whether a future matter, or words of the world, except words of Torah. And the general principle is that which we are required to accept."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 58, :notes {0 "Resolved יי as YHWH per divine name rules; the phrase משובב נתיבות likely alludes to a textual variant or parallel reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:14.955858978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}